# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the React + Vite project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` package using npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the resolved dependencies

### 2. Analytics Configuration
**File Modified:** `src/ClerkApp.jsx`
- Added import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `ClerkProvider` alongside the existing `<SpeedInsights />` component
- The Analytics component is now at the root level and will track all pages in the application

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I used the React-specific import path (`@vercel/analytics/react`) which is the correct approach for React + Vite projects.

The `<Analytics />` component was placed in `ClerkApp.jsx`, which serves as the root application component. This ensures analytics tracking across the entire application.

## Framework Compatibility

This implementation is specifically for:
- **Framework:** React 19.2.6
- **Build Tool:** Vite 8.0.12
- **Package Manager:** npm
- **Package:** `@vercel/analytics` (React import)

## Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linter ran - no new errors introduced (pre-existing lint warnings remain unchanged)
✅ Dependencies installed and lock file updated
✅ No tests available in project

## Next Steps

To enable Web Analytics data collection:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
3. After deployment, the system will automatically add routes at `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Notes

- The project already had `@vercel/speed-insights` installed, so the Analytics component was added alongside it
- Both Analytics and Speed Insights components work together to provide comprehensive observability
- Analytics is a separate product from Speed Insights and provides page view tracking and visitor analytics
